# Purpose
Implement reliable REST consumption with typed errors, safe logging, and clear UX for failed/offline states.

## Do / Don't

### DO
DO centralize all HTTP in a single client module; do not scatter fetch across components.
DO enforce HTTPS base URL via environment (e.g., NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL); no hardcoded secrets.
DO define a typed error model: `{ kind: 'network' | 'http' | 'parse'; status?: number; message: string; retriable?: boolean }`
DO provide offline/failed-network UX: clear message + retry action.
DO redact logs: no Authorization headers, tokens, cookies, PII (emails, phones, addresses).

### DON'T
MUST NOT log secrets or PII.
MUST NOT show raw server error payloads to users.
MUST NOT retry non-idempotent requests (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE) by default.

## Completion Checklist
[ ] REST calls go through one client module.
[ ] Typed error model; UX handles loading/error/offline states.
[ ] No secrets/PII in logs.
